Z||000003||Nashco||11-16-2001||12:26 AM||||I think the mirrors look sweet, and could look really good!  I'm a little worried that they wouldn't look right when you try to mount them.  For example, if you couldn't see too well when you made them at the right angle (look goofy at the best viewing angle); or, if there wasn't a very good mounting alternative and they look like they don't belong.<P>As far as the angle is concerned, the only reason that's an issue is because it doesn't look like the mirror faces themselves are adjustable, only the housing.  Is that right?  Oh, and these are real carbon fiber, not stickers, right?<P>Like I said, I really like the idea, but I'm too chicken to try something that expensive without seeing it first <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I'd probably be in for some if they looked right when mounted, but like I said...chicken!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||TRiAD||11-16-2001||10:03 AM||||Yes they're real, not stickers, and the whole housing turns. <P>They are designed to mount ahead of the driver (but on the door, like all mirrors) so the angle shouldn't be too extreme. <P>If Hybrid gets back to me, maybe he can take pics once his are mounted?<p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 11-16-2001).]||||reg||1
